&lt;h2 id="keynote-talks"&gt;Keynote talks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="ai-for-image-based-systems-biology-from-cryo-electron-tomography-to-virtual-spatial-transcriptomics"&gt;AI for Image-based Systems Biology: From Cryo-Electron Tomography to Virtual Spatial Transcriptomics&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tingying Peng&lt;/strong&gt; · Helmholtz Munich&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Workshops</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/workshops/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/workshops/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="workshops"&gt;Workshops&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on workshops run on Day 2 and Day 3. On Day 3, the opening session is plenary — for all participants — and the two later slots run as parallel tracks, so you can pick one in each. See the &lt;a href="https://scverse.org/conference2026/schedule/"&gt;schedule&lt;/a&gt; for timings and rooms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="from-data-to-insight-hands-on-with-sentira-single-cell"&gt;From Data to Insight: Hands-On with Sentira Single Cell&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10x Genomics&lt;/strong&gt; · Day 2&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join 10x Genomics for an exclusive, hands-on introduction to Sentira Single Cell — 10x Genomics&amp;rsquo; newly announced autonomous AI agent for Chromium analysis, designed to transform how you navigate high-dimensional omics data.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Registration</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/registration/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/registration/</guid><description>&lt;div class="status-banner"&gt;Registration has closed. We look forward to welcoming registered attendees in Copenhagen.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="registration"&gt;Registration&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Registration for scverse conference 2026 has closed. If you have a question about an existing registration, email &lt;a href="mailto:conference2026@scverse.org"&gt;conference2026@scverse.org&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sign up for announcements via &lt;a href="https://scverse.zulipchat.com/"&gt;Zulip&lt;/a&gt; or follow us on social media for the latest updates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="travel-grants"&gt;Travel grants&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to making the conference accessible to as many people as possible. As in previous years, we offered &lt;strong&gt;travel grants&lt;/strong&gt; to help cover registration, accommodation, and travel.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Call for proposals</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/call-for-proposals/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/call-for-proposals/</guid><description>&lt;div class="status-banner"&gt;Abstract submission closed on &lt;strong&gt;September 7, 2026&lt;/strong&gt;. Thank you to everyone who submitted.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="share-your-work"&gt;Share your work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scverse conference program is built with the community. The programme is built with contributions from researchers, developers, and users across the single-cell and spatial omics ecosystem. Submission types were:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="card-grid"&gt;
 &lt;div class="info-card"&gt;
 &lt;h3&gt;Talks&lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;Present your research, tool, or method as a contributed talk. Selected abstracts are scheduled across the main program.&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="info-card"&gt;
 &lt;h3&gt;Posters&lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;Share work in progress and connect with the community during dedicated poster sessions.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sponsors</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/sponsors/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/sponsors/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="our-sponsors"&gt;Our sponsors&lt;/h2&gt;
