&lt;h2 id="past-sponsors"&gt;Past sponsors&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Past scverse conference sponsors include the Chan Zuckerberg Initiative, CZ Biohub, 10x Genomics, Altos Labs, Immunai, Boehringer Ingelheim, Tahoe, Somite, TileDB, LatchBio, and Data Intuitive.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Venue &amp; travel</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/travel/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/travel/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;scverse conference 2026 · DTU Lyngby Campus, Kongens Lyngby · 12–14 October 2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="the-venue"&gt;The venue&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class="venue-addr"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DTU Lyngby Campus, Building 101&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Address: Anker Engelunds Vej 1, 2800 Kgs. Lyngby, Denmark.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="travel-map"&gt;&lt;iframe title="Map of DTU Lyngby Campus" loading="lazy" src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=Anker%20Engelunds%20Vej%201,%202800%20Kongens%20Lyngby&amp;z=14&amp;output=embed"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The campus sits about 15 km north of central Copenhagen, in Kongens Lyngby. There are two sensible approaches: stay locally in Lyngby, which gives you a short walk to the venue and quiet evenings, or stay in Copenhagen and travel in each morning, which takes roughly 40 minutes. Both work well. Lyngby has very few hotels, so if you want to be within walking distance, book early.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Code of Conduct</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/code-of-conduct/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/code-of-conduct/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This code of conduct was developed for the scverse conferences. For more details, see the full &lt;a href="https://scverse.org/about/code_of_conduct"&gt;scverse Code of Conduct&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="our-pledge"&gt;Our pledge&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We as members, contributors, and leaders pledge to make participation in our community a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, body size, visible or invisible disability, ethnicity, sex characteristics, gender identity and expression, level of experience, education, socio-economic status, nationality, personal appearance, race, caste, color, religion, or sexual identity and orientation.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Organizers</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/organizers/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/organizers/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="organizing-committee"&gt;Organizing committee&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scverse conference 2026 is organized by members of the &lt;a href="https://scverse.org/people"&gt;scverse community&lt;/a&gt;, together with our local partners at DTU, Copenhagen. scverse is a community-developed, non-profit project, fiscally sponsored by &lt;a href="https://numfocus.org/project/scverse"&gt;NumFOCUS&lt;/a&gt;. The conference is run by the people who build and maintain the ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
